; REFUSED BY DEFAULT SINCE 2026-08-31, which is this file's whole point.
; ADR 0019 makes an integer operation the compiler cannot prove stays inside
; the portable window a COMPILE ERROR, so `cmd/build` now declines this
; program by name and operation instead of emitting code that wraps on Go
; and the JVM and loses precision on V8. `-checked` still builds it, taking
; the trap: that is the second escape, and it is what this program is for.
;
; Iterative Fibonacci — which TERMINATES but whose accumulator provably does
; not stay in the portable window.
;
; fib(79) is 14472334024676221, past 2^53. So a correct analysis proves the loop
; stops and refuses to bound `a` and `b`, and an exact-integer representation
; would have to check those two additions. It is the case where the answer is
; "yes it terminates, and no you cannot have the fast representation".

(use go)
(export fib)

(sig fib ((n int)) int (where (and (<= 0 n) (< n 1000))))

(def fib (fn (n)
  (loop ((a 0) (b 1) (i 0))
    (go.>= i n)  a
    else         (again b (go.+ a b) (go.+ i 1)))))
